{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qwe6jfjguvq2wvvkoeq7clczpzbtdi32uqsckpt74ziowy4grwqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **One real bug found and fixed.**\n\n## Bug fixed in the Rust translation\n`src/lib.rs` used hand-written `strlen`/`strrchr`/`memcpy`. Under `-C debug-assertions` (the `dev` profile) Rust's raw-pointer UB checks fire on a null dereference and `abort()` → **SIGABRT (6)**, while the C faults with **SIGSEGV (11)**. Four error-path tests (`ERRORS.md` E4/E8/E9/E10) caught it in the debug profile only. Fixed by importing `strlen`, `strrchr`, `memcpy` from libc — the exact symbols the C calls — and switching `ptr::add` → `wrapping_add` so no Rust-only bounds/provenance requirement is imposed where the C has none (e.g. `separator == 0`, which legitimately returns a pointer one past the NUL).\n\n## Completion gate\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — `nm -D` diff is empty; both `extractFilename` and `FIO_createFilename_fromOutDir` exported. No untranslated C module (`src/lib.c` is the only TU). 0 unresolved non-libc symbols; Rust imports the same `calloc`/`exit`/`fprintf`/`strerror` as C, so returned buffers stay `free()`-able.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 27 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass, ~400 randomized inputs each (fixed seed), driving the low-level `extractFilename` directly as well as the wrapper, plus a composed-pipeline row. The **entire `calloc`ed buffer** is compared, including the `suffixLen` zero padding.\n- [x] **Binary stdout** — N/A (no `add_executable`/`main()`/`[[bin]]`). The library's only stream output, the `fprintf(stderr, …)` on alloc failure, is compared byte-for-byte via a pipe.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 16 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, incl. `exit(30)` + stderr text, `size_t` wrap-around (both the \"still huge → exit(30)\" and \"wraps tiny → succeeds\" sides), the OOB `outDirName[-1]` read with a *controlled* preceding byte, null pointers, and out-of-range separator values passed as full `c_int` (`0x100`, `-1`, `i32::MIN/MAX`).\n- [x] **All feature combinations** — crate declares no `[features]`, so `run_verification.sh` runs the power set (`<default>`, `--no-default-features`) × both profiles = 4 configs; 46 tests pass in each.\n\nTwo harness pitfalls also fixed: `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`, so a stale-`.so` guard now aborts the run if either library predates its sources — without it the suite silently passed 5 injected mutations. A 7-mutation check now confirms the suite detects separator inversion, off-by-one sizes, `NULL` returns, wrong exit codes, and `malloc`-instead-of-`calloc`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":110307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":688,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7946095f-9f6e-4726-b7a6-ad237fbdc280","uuid":"5ea4fbd8-68fc-4bad-b495-362b7580749b","timestamp":"2026-09-05T10:48:55.080Z"}
